        "original_id": "ca0e90e0-327e-5dad-a669-add4e9425f73",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Frideric Handel\n- Works: Sosarme, re di Media; Sosarmes, King of Media\n- Places: London; King's Theatre in the Haymarket; Halle; Hamburg; Italy\n- Topics: opera; baroque music; naturalisation\n\nFacts:\n- George Frideric Handel was born as Georg Friedrich Händel on 23 February 1685 O.S. / 5 March 1685 N.S.\n- George Frideric Handel received important training in Halle and later worked as a composer in Hamburg and Italy.\n- George Frideric Handel settled in London in 1712.\n- George Frideric Handel became a naturalised British subject in 1727.\n- In 1732, George Frideric Handel wrote the opera Sosarme, re di Media for the King's Theatre in the Haymarket, London.\n- Sosarme, re di Media, also titled \"Sosarmes, King of Media\" and catalogued as HWV 30, ran for 12 performances at the King's Theatre in the Haymarket, London.\n- George Frideric Handel was a German, later British, baroque composer who became well known for his operas, oratorios, anthems, and organ concertos.\n- George Frideric Handel spent the bulk of his career in London and died on 14 April 1759.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
